    "done_when": "when reckon/_backends.py _seed_harness_entry copies the operator's settings.json hooks key into a run's harness home, the copied hooks pass through reckon/hooks/install.py's recogniser and composer (the functions reckon sync's configure_crew_guards already uses), so every reckon hook command in the run home is interpreter-bound whatever the operator file holds, hooks that are not reckon's are copied byte-for-byte, and the operator's own file is never written; tests/test_run_home_hooks_are_interpreter_bound.py seeds a run home from a temporary operator settings file holding bare reckon hook commands beside a hook that is not reckon's and finds the run home's reckon commands interpreter-bound, the other hook unchanged and the operator file's bytes unchanged, and seeds from a file already holding the bound commands and finds the run home identical to it; no test reads or writes the real ~/.claude; gate, run serially: /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider --basetemp=/dev/shm/run-home-hooks-bound tests/test_run_home_hooks_are_interpreter_bound.py tests/test_harness_home_carries_the_operator_config.py tests/test_harness_home_carries_mcp_servers.py tests/test_reckon_hook_commands.py tests/test_hook_installer.py exits 0",
